  </div>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <p class="eyebrow">How they help</p>
  <h2 class="sec">Every project has to earn its cost claim.</h2>
  <p>A project only counts as a cost-reduction path where energy, capital, maintenance, and local conditions make a net reduction plausible. Where the model shows it doesn’t beat the status quo, we publish that negative result too. Where a cost driver is policy rather than technology, our role is open data and nonpartisan analysis — never partisan lobbying.</p>
</section>

<section class="blk blk--cream2">
  <p class="eyebrow">Longer horizon</p>
  <h2 class="sec">Later — gated on funding and safety.</h2>
  <p>Longer-term studies and partner-led physical demonstrations stay research-and-design tracks until there is funding, a local operator, safety review, legal capacity, insurance, and site permissions. None of it involves Uncost directly providing healthcare, care, child-facing education, or safety services.</p>
